  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "9e4249bc-8c6b-4a91-88b7-38a968d518d6",
    "name": "PetStore",
    "description": "## PetStore API – Test Collection\n\nThis collection covers functional testing of the **PetStore API**, organized into three main modules:\n\n---\n\n### 🐾 Pets\n\nTests for the pet management endpoints (`/pet`). Divided into:\n\n- **Positivo**: happy-path flows — create, retrieve, upload photo, update, and delete a pet, including a follow-up query to confirm deletion.\n    \n- **Negativo**: error-path scenarios — invalid ID, invalid body on creation, editing or deleting a non-existent pet.\n    \n\n---\n\n### 👤 Usuários (Users)\n\nTests for the user management endpoints (`/user`). Divided into:\n\n- **Positivo**: create a user and retrieve it by username.\n    \n- **Negativo**: validation failures — empty body, empty username, invalid email, empty password, and duplicate username (two separate attempts).\n    \n\n---\n\n### 🏪 Loja (Store)\n\nTests for the store/order endpoints (`/store`). Divided into:\n\n- **Setup**: creates a pet to be used in order tests.\n    \n- **Positivo**: check inventory, place an order, retrieve it, delete it, and confirm deletion.\n    \n- **Negativo**: query with invalid order ID, create an order with invalid data, and delete a non-existent order.\n    \n\n---\n\n### Variables\n\nAll requests rely on the **PetStore** environment, which provides `{{url_base}}` and dynamic variables such as `{{created_id}}`, `{{created_username}}`, and `{{created_order_id}}` that are populated by pre-request or test scripts during the collection run.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "57917096",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/57917096-9e4249bc-8c6b-4a91-88b7-38a968d518d6?source=collection_link"
  },
